# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Activating an ability whose cost sacrifices its source does not ask for a second confirmation.
# Forcing: Evolving Wilds is the only available action with a self-sacrifice cost.
# AI behavior: The scenario ends after the human resolves the search, before the opponent makes a decision.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = The activation reaches library search and puts the chosen Forest onto the battlefield.
#   LOSE = The activation or search did not complete before the turn limit.
#   TIMEOUT = Cost payment stalled on an extra confirmation.
# Card roles:
#   Evolving Wilds — supplies the self-sacrifice activation cost.
#   Forest — supplies the only legal search result.
#   Mountain — keeps the opponent library non-empty.
# Protocol path: ActionsAvailableReq activation, Sacrifice zone transfer, SearchReq, then resolution without an extra internal confirmation.

[metadata]
Name:Sacrifice Cost Confirm
Goal:Survive
Turns:3
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Pay a sacrifice-self activation cost and resolve the resulting search.

